    dc:type "resolution-route/proof";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Check an explicit Diophantine encoding of rule 110 evolution, the proof of rule 110 universality, and the logical reduction from effective arithmetic expressiveness to incompleteness under the required consistency assumptions. A failed encoding or invalid implication refutes this proposed derivation, while a verified chain confirms it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "An exponential Diophantine equation is not automatically an ordinary polynomial equation.", "Gödel incompleteness requires consistency and effective axiomatizability assumptions.", "Universality alone must be linked carefully to representability and provability.";
